Z||000000||DR650SE||10-29-2001||01:51 PM||||Has anyone ever driven an Acura NSX?  How does it compare to a Fiero?  Got numbers?  Just curious cuz I sorta like the car and so does my bro.  I don't think they are woth the price, but I still like them.<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||5
Z||000001||Don_Chi_Chi||10-29-2001||02:12 PM||||Probably like hopping in a Super Beetle and then jumping in an 88 GT and comparing the differences.  The NSX's got a great engine, japanese or not and can handle like its on rails.  Its styling is a little old now though.  <P>------------------<BR>Previously known as Saleenfiero||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||10-29-2001||02:21 PM||||I haven't driven one, but I love them.  They look like they could be a mid-90's Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>And I saw a video of an NSX and a Ferrari F355 racing.  The NSX won the quarter mile.  Barely - but it did win.  They didn't list the times, just showed them crossing the finish line.  The NSX was a nose ahead of the Ferrari.||||reg||10
Z||000003||Brian87egotrip||10-29-2001||02:54 PM||||I drove one the nite before I left for run for the hills. I looked at the owner as I was doing 105 and told him he just ruined the trip for me. What a nice ride. Only thing is all the power is in the high revs. Handles unbelievably well. <P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sage||10-29-2001||03:55 PM||||Never driven one, but encountered one on the interstate once.  He got up next to me like he wanted to play a little.  So I took my stock 87GT with 177,000 mi. on the clock, up to 110mph, at which point, cruising right along side me, he just goosed it what seemed like a little bit...and he was gone!  Didn't take him 60 seconds either!  LOL<P>With the looks, performance and price, I think they just about qualify as an "exotic".<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChopTop||10-29-2001||04:04 PM||||They are also receiving a face lift this year since they are nearing the end of the platforms cycle.  I've seen a couple of artist renderings of the next NSX, if they are anything close they will be much more exotic looking.  ||||reg||1
