Z||000007||TRiAD||10-29-2001||04:32 PM||||I occasionally have used examples from $25K on up. <P>New ones are in the upper $80Ks. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000008||btoth||10-29-2001||04:40 PM||||Yeah, about the price of a Lotus Esprit.  I'd rather have a nice black Lotus V8.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <I>Dreaming...</I>||||reg||1
Z||000009||AkursedX||10-29-2001||08:10 PM||||It seems like I am one of the privleged to have driven both an Acura NSX and a Lotus Espirt turbo (Just a 4-cyl though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> )<P>In comparison to my 88GT (Poly, lowered, KYB's, super stiff) my GT handled better than both of those cars at low speeds, but ride comfort is also a hell of alot worse.<P>When getting up into higher speeds, the NSX is alot more stable, then the Fiero, then the Lotus.  (I really wasn't too impressed with the Lotus.)  But I have no numbers or anything.<P>In conclusion, a Fiero can easily be made to handle as well as either of these supercars, but you will pay for it in ride comfort.<P>Hope this helps.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||varnster||10-29-2001||10:00 PM||||Your looking at around 88 grand for the nsx<BR>0-60 in 4sec, o-120 in just under 11sec. A<BR>VERY VERY FAST CAR. It is a touch faster then<BR>the vette (For the moment) but the vette is<BR>about 35 grand cheaper. As far as campared to<BR>our beloved fiero, get real! We love our cars<BR>but its not even in the ballpark. I saw this<BR>show this weekend I think CAR AND DRIVER and <BR>they talked about it. I had no idea they were so pricey.||||reg||9
Z||000011||Formula||10-29-2001||10:16 PM||||o-120 in just under 11sec<P>does that mean they run at least an 11 sec qtr mile..........  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Formula_sigx21.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||AutoXdbdragSE||10-29-2001||10:26 PM||||the only similarity between the car's is where the engine is, number of wheels, and number of seats.  Get real..  sure a fiero with LOTS of mods can maybe keep up.. but NSX's are race cars, it's just not a comparison. it's like asking how does a yugo compare to a integra type-R||||reg||1
Z||000013||California Kid||10-29-2001||11:08 PM||||I'm a little confused about some of the performance figures quoted above. Can someone explain how an NSX that weighs 3,069 lbs with max factory horse of 290 turn 0 to 60 in 4sec, and 0 to 120 in under 11 sec.??<P>I've never seen one that fast and have beaten a couple of them.||||reg||1
Z||000014||fieroX||10-30-2001||02:40 AM||||NSX's run mid 13's, big deal.  I think it was probably a typo, maybe to 100 in 11 seconds, but probably close to 15 seconds to 120.  I do like the styling of the NSX though.  Hope to line up against one some day.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>previously known as pontiacs4me for the first 500 posts.||||reg||1
Z||000015||artherd||10-30-2001||03:27 AM||||The owner of one of the companies I consult for has a nice '94(I belive it's a 94...) black NSX.   Incredible car, the 3.0 (later cars get a 3200cc version) litre v6 is built using titanium connecting rods (like a certin Italian carmaker's blinkin awesome 3500cc 5-valve V8...)<P>Anyway, it sounds like a Honda engine...<BR>A FORMULA ONE Honda engine (above about 6,000 or so. Wowie.)<P>Handles great, of course, however, so do our cars (God, THANK YOU for the mid-engine layout!!!)  <P>The NSX is incredibly stable at speeds a stock Fiero can't dream of however, and it's just an order of magnitude smoother, faster, and slicker through the air.<P>It does everything better than any stock Fiero, so much better infact that it actually feels.... well, less than entirely eventful.  Iike how a BMW 5-series is such a damn good car that 110mph feels as relaxed and leasurly as 70mph in anything else...<P>Intresting fact, the stock tyres the 94 came with must be 90% paste, they're grippy, but are GONE inside of 8kmiles. (and the NSX is not terribly powerful a car, so it's not exactly chewing them up with 7,000 clutch dumps.  Or wait, was that me...  <P>If I had to pick an exotic car (and it certinly and absolutely **IS** an exotic, a damned fine one at that, and you can pick up an older model for around $30k...) to commute in every day, it would HANDS DOWN be an Acura/Honda NSX.<P>Imagine our cars with (much) better build quality, and an engine swap from an Honda F1 car.  That's an NSX.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000016||DR650SE||10-30-2001||08:11 AM||||When I went to Lodon in the summer I saw a few NSX's and they all had honda badging.  So why the differance here in the states?<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||10
Z||000017||TRiAD||10-30-2001||09:05 AM||||Acura only exists in the States...it's Honda everywhere else...<P><BR>NUMBERS:<P><BR>$88,066; 0-60 4.9; 0-100 11.9; 1/4mi 13.3@108.1; top 168; 60-0 134'; 80-0 220'; skid 0.92g; slalom 62.1mph; 20.8mpg. <P>R&T 7-98. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAlAL0S2vLvViYU9P7uloj72fLFTqfz59trng8I7AOG7hGCvfk6WP96n!gnOaEUAvooy1kUoWucv7BJ7L5EWg/temp-sig.gif">    <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000018||yo_sweet||10-30-2001||09:20 AM||||i saw a race somewhere on the net where a 93 nsx was racing a 440-six pack 71 road runner , it was a street race the road runner won by soemthin around 3 car lenths , there was a biography on this program , and supposidly lots of people where hit by these guys raceing on this one street<P>apple's and oranges?||||reg||7
Z||000019||Slammed Fiero||10-30-2001||09:34 AM||||Must have been one hell of a modded road runner. My dads friend has a 95. Occasionally he comes to the track with it to play. Nice car , pretty quick . But for my 88  grand (135 Grand in canada)I want something a weee bit faster. Espically from a company that extracts 240hp from a 4cyl , but gives me an anemic 290hp from a Vtec 6cyl.<P>The chassis and aluminum work is nothing short of amazing. The styling is getting a bit dated.<P>The price says supercar.. the performance doesn't. Just an expensive sports car. The NSX is all about Finess and balance. I want excess!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, Big Bore TB, 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000020||falconhulk||10-30-2001||10:37 AM||||You guys know the engine was civic based parts.  All except the block.  No joke look it up.  They are not faster then current vettes (Z06).  They were when the platform was new.  Current speculation is that then new one will be 8cyl and pretty much be 2 back to back twin turbo civic engines.  BTW I have not seen a used one for below $55k.  <P>[This message has been edited by falconhulk To reflect Triads request).]<p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||TRiAD||10-30-2001||11:30 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by falconhulk:<BR><B>You guys know they use civic engine parts right?  All except the block are stock civic parts.  No joke look it up.  They are not faster then current vettes.  They were when the platform was new.  Current speculation is that then new one will be 8cyl and pretty much be 2 back to back twin turbo civic engines.  BTW I have not seen a used one for below $55k.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>There are no swappable parts in the C30A1 3.0 DOHC VTEC V6 and ANY of the i-4s, the D16s, B16As, B18C1, B18C5, the H22s, the A20s, F20s, B20s, none of them. Not one part.<P>Also, they outrun EVERY current production Vette except the Z06. Check Road & Track magazine's Road Test Summary...<P>Since you've never seen one under $55K, here's just a few...... <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+A0+R100000407+Q254415425" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+A0+R100000407+Q254415425</A>  <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R1247030+Q254415425" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R1247030+Q254415425</A>  <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R514671341+Q254415425" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R514671341+Q254415425</A>  <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R514671341+Q254415425" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R514671341+Q254415425</A>  <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R514671341+Q254415425" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R514671341+Q254415425</A>  <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R1232455+Q254415425" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R1232455+Q254415425</A>  <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R514670641+Q254415425" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R514670641+Q254415425</A>  <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R514670641+Q254415425" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R514670641+Q254415425</A>  <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R100000770+Q254415425" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R100000770+Q254415425</A>  <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R512295870+Q254415425" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R512295870+Q254415425</A>  <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R512295870+Q254415425" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R512295870+Q254415425</A>  <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R512295870+Q254415425" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R512295870+Q254415425</A>  <A HREF="http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R1200128+Q254415425" TARGET=_blank>http://www.classifieds2000.com/cgi-cls/ad.exe?P1+C14+R1200128+Q254415425</A> <P>This is only about 1/2 of them listed, and that was with a 2 second search. This is not ebay, these are sell prices. <P>Sorry , had a bad day and those statements pulled the pin.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I'll switch back to decaf now. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
