Z||000028||Slammed Fiero||10-30-2001||01:38 PM||||I could be wrong but...<P>Didn't they just up the HP in the NSX recently? I can remember competing in Pro solo (drag race up ..autocross back) against a few NSX's and never had a problem outlaunching them or beating them with an L98 Vette.<P>If my memory serves me correctly (and if It doesn't I have the magazine) The earlier cars only posted 6.2 to 6.4 sec to sixty.<P>I believe they had 250hp.. Not completley sure. I do have the road and track article somewhere here. They tested an MR2 Turbo , NSX , Mitsu 3000GT Vr4 and something else. For the money the MR2 was the best buy , by far. It was faster to 60 than the NSX (5.99 for the Mr2 turbo)<P>No need to beat a dead horse. NSX is a great car in need of some bigger HP #'s to justify the price. Surely honda can pull a streetable 350-400hp out of a Vtec 6.<P>I just wonder why everyone thinks the Z06 is some sort of a bench mark.. I like vettes , We have a vette. But the quality , feel and precision doesn't compare to some German counterparts. Although the price is about 1/2<P>Jonathan McCreery||||reg||1
Z||000029||yo_sweet||10-30-2001||01:45 PM||||the plymoth 71 road runner was pushing soemthing along the lines of 500hp+ no NOS<BR>i always thought the old mopars where pretty fast? even the daytonas from the 80s with the turbo IIs were quicker then our v6? although the laser with the turbo I was only 140hp but it was a 4cyl||||reg||
Z||000030||falconhulk||10-30-2001||02:03 PM||||yeah yo sweet.  the dodge turbo1=140hp, turbo2=174hp and turbo3=225.  Turbo 2 and up were great engines!  Those stock Hp can be raied way up by increasing the boost.||||reg||1
Z||000031||sloth85GT||10-30-2001||02:18 PM||||For the cost of an NSX, it's a waste. I hate Honda cars with a passion, they're scared to use some REAL horsepower. If they put a V8 in it, I'm sure it would be a 3.6L V8 or something like that so that it can be "ecenomical". It's not a super car, a super car is one that tops out about 400HP stock and can turn on a dime. All in can do is the turning part. The chassis has potential, they had to screw it up with a V6. For people that want to buy NSX's, get a Viper! Or even a Vetter and go see Mr. Lingenfelter with your extra cash.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">      <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<p>[This message has been edited by sloth85GT (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000032||TylerB11||10-30-2001||02:28 PM||||sloth - more cylinder doesn't always mean more gooder. <BR>For example The v12 Viper vs the f6 Porche 911 turbo. The current Ruf version of the porche's flat-6 (RUF CTR) outputs over 500 hp. How many cylinders are in an indy car?<P>point made.||||reg||1
Z||000033||falconhulk||10-30-2001||03:03 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by TylerB11:<BR><B>sloth - more cylinder doesn't always mean more gooder. <BR>For example The v12 Viper vs the f6 Porche 911 turbo. The current Ruf version of the porche's flat-6 (RUF CTR) outputs over 500 hp. How many cylinders are in an indy car?<P>point made.</B>[/QUOTE<BR>An formula car can produce massive amounts of HP but the TQ is low.  Some cars have to be push started becasue the motor can spin real fast (High HP) but not produce enough tQ to get it rolling.  <P>heh heh that statement going to get a bunch of bad replys or what?<p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000034||yo_sweet||10-30-2001||03:20 PM||||btw i remeber reading soemthing on ls1.com about the 98 and up t/a's beating the nsx is this true?||||reg||1
Z||000035||Slammed Fiero||10-30-2001||03:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sloth85GT:<BR><B>For the cost of an NSX, it's a waste. I hate Honda cars with a passion, they're scared to use some REAL horsepower. If they put a V8 in it, I'm sure it would be a 3.6L V8 or something like that so that it can be "ecenomical". It's not a super car, a super car is one that tops out about 400HP stock and can turn on a dime. All in can do is the turning part. The chassis has potential, they had to screw it up with a V6. For people that want to buy NSX's, get a Viper! Or even a Vetter and go see Mr. Lingenfelter with your extra cash.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Weeeewww there doggy.. A viper.. A Fiberglass TUB. Heavy cars that understeer and that are BIG. Not exactly a supercar. As for the 3.6ltr V8 comment. Look at Ferrari's ..The essence of supercar. Small high winding motors with progressive powerbands. (read never ending) (360 modena 4 cam 5 valve V8)<P><BR>In the realm of supercar Cubic inches don't matter. I know of quite a few naturally aspirated 911's that would lay a roal ass whooping on a Viper or a Z06, and drive home.<P><BR>Yeah the NSX lacks overall hp and performance #'s. But the technology and balance of the car is perfect. The chassis design rivals the vipers or the Vettes..easily<P>how is a viper impressive?<P>488 Cu in and only 450hp?<P>I will post the article later tonight. Yahoo groups isn't working right now. One of the engineers in our club got some information comparing motors and HP produced. A Viper motor is pathetic when it comes to Hp vs Size. Yeah it's a torque monster and it lays down some impressive straight line #'s. But if I want straight line i will go get a 71 Nova and shove a big block in it.<P>I urge you to go watch a viper at a track, a street one , hell even an ACR. Any track that has any sort of technical aspect to it and the viper will be roasting it's brakes and tires pretty quick. <P>JM <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000036||artherd||10-30-2001||04:21 PM||||Hmmm..... look for a 3.6 litre V8 in the Ferrari 360 Modena.   It puts out 394bhp.  Revs to 8750 and makes torque *all over* and never quits!     <P>If that car dosen't move you, then you need to get to a shop and have your SOUL examined  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>The viper looks kinda cool, and you have to admit Chrysler has Hudgbah for producing it.  However, it's a big, old, truck frame housing a motor that's big, but little else can be said for it.  Great for burnouts, but not a lot else.   Loves to *MELT* brakes (worse than even pre88 Fieros).    It's a Hot Rod, (and a cool one) but not by my definition, a supercar.<P>PS: I didn't think that ~450lb-ft would ever be considered 'low' torque.... (most F1 motors make around that much torque...  of course, doing it at 17,000rpm makes for about 900-1200bhp.   <P>Yeah, they will stall *really* easially.  (though they are push-started BECAUSE THE CARS HAVE NO STARTER. Weight savings.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   4 or 5 (or more) puck clutches are basically a binary operation, on or off.    And the torque is up high, where it's useable. (so you're left trying to bust loose 20" wide gumball slicks with an engine with almost no rotational innertia, and a toggle-switch for a clutch...)   I don't laugh at the guys who stall in the pits anymore  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>PS: Today's F1 motors are V10s.  Everything from turbo v6s to turbo Flat-12s have been competitive, depending on the year (and regs)<P><BR>Jonothan, you said it best about the NSX. <BR>It's almost too *easy*.  I want excess too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sloth85GT:<BR><B>For the cost of an NSX, it's a waste. I hate Honda cars with a passion, they're scared to use some REAL horsepower. If they put a V8 in it, I'm sure it would be a 3.6L V8 or something like that so that it can be "ecenomical". It's not a super car, a super car is one that tops out about 400HP stock and can turn on a dime. All in can do is the turning part. The chassis has potential, they had to screw it up with a V6. For people that want to buy NSX's, get a Viper! Or even a Vetter and go see Mr. Lingenfelter with your extra cash.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000037||falconhulk||10-30-2001||04:41 PM||||By low TQ I meant some of the super eff turbo 4 cyl make 800hp but have 120lb TQ.  And they have to rev high to get there.  Yes the new motors have TQ throught the pband.  What I was trying to say that a 400hp motor with 395lb TQ is a better street car then the mentioned 500HP motor with a small lesser amount of TQ on the street.  A Formula engine is not real ideal for street use.  Although it could be made to be.  Dont you just love those little 1.6 liter masterpieces? ||||reg||1
Z||000038||California Kid||10-30-2001||05:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by falconhulk:<BR><B>By low TQ I meant some of the super eff turbo 4 cyl make 800hp but have 120lb TQ.  And they have to rev high to get there.  Yes the new motors have TQ throught the pband.  What I was trying to say that a 400hp motor with 395lb TQ is a better street car then the mentioned 500HP motor with a small lesser amount of TQ on the street.  A Formula engine is not real ideal for street use.  Although it could be made to be.  Dont you just love those little 1.6 liter masterpieces? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>*********************************************<BR>You mean like this??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engine_small.jpg"> <BR>400hp  390 torque<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_7.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000039||TRiAD||10-30-2001||05:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sloth85GT:<BR><B>For the cost of an NSX, it's a waste. I hate Honda cars with a passion, they're scared to use some REAL horsepower. If they put a V8 in it, I'm sure it would be a 3.6L V8 or something like that so that it can be "ecenomical". It's not a super car, a super car is one that tops out about 400HP stock and can turn on a dime. All in can do is the turning part. The chassis has potential, they had to screw it up with a V6. For people that want to buy NSX's, get a Viper! Or even a Vetter and go see Mr. Lingenfelter with your extra cash.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ferrari's aren't supercars, since they can make HP w/out using big blocks? Sure.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000040||TRiAD||10-30-2001||05:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TylerB11:<BR><B>sloth - more cylinder doesn't always mean more gooder. <BR>For example The v12 Viper vs the f6 Porche 911 turbo. The current Ruf version of the porche's flat-6 (RUF CTR) outputs over 500 hp. How many cylinders are in an indy car?<P>point made.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, point made, but the Viper has an aluminum V10, no V12. You're the 18th person to post this here, where did this V12 stuff come from?!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000041||TRiAD||10-30-2001||05:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by falconhulk:<BR><B>An formula car can produce massive amounts of HP but the TQ is low.  Some cars have to be push started becasue the motor can spin real fast (High HP) but not produce enough tQ to get it rolling.  <P>heh heh that statement going to get a bunch of bad replys or what?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh, yeah. I always see the pit crew out there push-starting the F1 cars as they run 0-60 in about a half a heartbeat off the line, since they can only run 200MPH and can't get out of their own way off the line...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000042||falconhulk||10-30-2001||05:20 PM||||triad depends on which formula circuit you watch.  As stated earlier some dont have starters.  Some tracks forbid push starting also.  Some of the older and espically the hyper efficent 4cyl cars had to be push started.  The reason I put that at the end was i knew it would raise a comment from you and was trolling for ya....relax I was just fooling a round!||||reg||1
Z||000043||TRiAD||10-30-2001||05:22 PM||||I really like it here, and I usually enjoy the intelligent discussion, but there has been a lot of ignorance shown lately. <P>Canwe PLEASE look-up our info before we go spouting off what some 14-year-old brat said in homeroom like it's gospel?<P>We are all enthusiasts here, and we're all here to learn from and help eachother, but BAD INFO can be dangerous. PLEASE be sure before you post an opinion as fact. <P>BTW, the NSX started with 270HP and now has 320. FYI. ||||reg||1
Z||000044||TRiAD||10-30-2001||05:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by falconhulk:<BR><B>triad depends on which formula circuit you watch.  As stated earlier some dont have starters.  Some tracks forbid push starting also.  Some of the older and espically the hyper efficent 4cyl cars had to be push started.  The reason I put that at the end was i knew it would raise a comment from you and was trolling for ya....relax I was just fooling a round!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Most F1 cars do not have starters on board, they use a portable starter that is hitched to the back temporarilly. I've never seen one push-started unless it was stalled on a pit stop. <BR>It has NOTHING to do with low-end torque, but with wanting the car to be lighter. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000045||falconhulk||10-30-2001||05:36 PM||||Ok, Triad, I am completely aware of this.  Like I said I was just trying to get a rise out of YOU becasue of what happened earlier.  man whats going on with you???  never read a thread where you acted like this before.||||reg||1
Z||000046||TRiAD||10-30-2001||06:00 PM||||My response to you was civil, wasn't it? Crap, I must be raggin.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>I was just saying that it wasn't torque, only weight concerns, sorry if I sounded (?) mad or something. ||||reg||1
Z||000047||Mickey_Moose||10-30-2001||06:14 PM||||We have a fellow here in Edmonton that shows up to race his NSX on the Slalom courses. It's fairly quick, but as was meantioned earlier, it's power range is in the high rpms. He is one of the quicker cars that race...but he has a hard time keeping up with a couple of 911 Turbos that comes out from time to time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Tim<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000048||Slammed Fiero||10-30-2001||06:38 PM||||In an average F1 engine, running at 18,000 rpm (300 revs per second), each spark plug fires 30 times a second. <P>An n/a 3.0lt  V-10 F1 engine produces about 280 hp/L on 97-octane unleaded pump gas. <P>A Dodge Viper 8.0L V-10 produces only 56 hp/L <P> an IRL 3.5L V-8 about 185 hp/L<BR>on methanol.<BR>    <BR>At 17 or 18000 RPM those pistons change direction about 500 times<BR>per second.  They said the wrist pins undergo somewhere around 8000 Gs<BR>of force at that speed.<P>Dug this up from an article posted on my autocross list.<P>GOOOO VIPER...!!!<P>A fiero makes 50Hp per liter.<P>So again I state.. GOOO Viper!!<P>JM <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000049||danny boy||10-30-2001||10:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B> Canwe PLEASE look-up our info before we go spouting off what some 14-year-old brat said in homeroom like it's gospel?<P>We are all enthusiasts here, and we're all here to learn from and help eachother, but BAD INFO can be dangerous. PLEASE be sure before you post an opinion as fact. <P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Quit Magazine racing. R&T don't know crap, especially in the Qtr. mile. On another post here somewhere, somebody was running low 15s in a stock Fiero. According to magazines, no stock Fiero runs that. I saw a Stock 'Vette('00) run a 12.98. Completely stock. R&T says it'll do what-13.6? I don't think so. Then take into account what automakers influence does to a magazine's reporting, and you have no solid ground except its on paper.If they print it it must be true, right? Yeah, like everything you see on the internet.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000050||danny boy||10-30-2001||10:40 PM|||| Slammed, I'd like to add a HP to liter figure,too. My 3.0L TT V6 makes somewhere in the neighborhood of 130HP/L.<BR>Now if I could just get that out of the Fiero. STUPID GM ENGINEERING!!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000051||TRiAD||10-31-2001||12:27 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy:<BR><B> Quit Magazine racing. R&T don't know crap, especially in the Qtr. mile. On another post here somewhere, somebody was running low 15s in a stock Fiero. According to magazines, no stock Fiero runs that. I saw a Stock 'Vette('00) run a 12.98. Completely stock. R&T says it'll do what-13.6? I don't think so. Then take into account what automakers influence does to a magazine's reporting, and you have no solid ground except its on paper.If they print it it must be true, right? Yeah, like everything you see on the internet.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Believe what you want. Any time I've tested a car in the same conditions and level of tune as R&T, I've come very close. You can say all you want, but I'll take my experiences, and an internationally published magazine over your "my car can do 0-60 3 seconds faster than they say" crap. <BR>BTW, You're a big Rush Limbaugh fan, aren't you? ...Or are you EdsB52 in disguise?!<BR>"It's all a conspiracy". whatever. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000052||Slammed Fiero||10-31-2001||01:24 AM||||I'm gonna stay out of this one to a certian degree.<P>Look at who advertises in magazines..the manufacturers.. they pay the bills. There is a LOT of hype surrounding magazines , their there as a sales medium to sell cars. There great to read and I buy a ton of them. But there not a Bible to go by.<P>Damm I need to find that up in smoke article about magazines.<P>They use quite a few tricks to get #'s. How about when the Z06 Came out and GM had all sorts of Ads in magazines saying 13.0 in the 1/4 mile..in the same magazine a road test yielded 12.5's??<P>Or when the Zr1 vette first came out..0 to 60 4.3 according to R&T . Corvette Fever does a test and all they can muster out of 3 different Zr1's in 5.0 sec.<P>HMMMmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm<P>I know you put a lot of faith in magazines triad , but there's a lot that goes in that isn't said. <P>Now back to the topic. The NSX is a great car for $45,000 , But at 90,000 I would expect to get a free S2000 with every purchase.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000053||DKOV||10-31-2001||12:17 PM||||In my opinion, if anyone cares, there are only TWO cars that deliver the kind of performance we are talking about at a price we can all live with...<P>Lotus and Fiero.<P>On the high end, a Lotus can be had for under $25,000 and will rip the head off ANY Acura NSX (or virtually any other car) and never look back.<P>A Fiero, on the other end, can be had for CHEAP and upgraded to a fire breathing monster for nodda...<P>In either case, 300 + HP and 0-60 times of 4 seconds are NOT uncommon.<P>Why waste one's money on a Nussance, I mean NSX, when what you want has been with us all this time?<P>Of course, with a Lotus, you also get Supercar status  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Speaking from experience because I have both... and you know what?  That are ALMOST the same car.  Give or take 60 + MPH on the high end and another full G in cornering coutesy of the Lotus  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Check one out!<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000054||MinnGreenGT||10-31-2001||12:22 PM||||DKOV- Just wondering what kind of Lotus you have...?  I'd love to have an Elise, but the only way to get one in the US is with a big pocketbook and an Acura V-Tec Motor (damn).||||reg||1
Z||000055||DKOV||10-31-2001||01:14 PM||||Esprit Turbo SE.<P>I hear, (from the Lotus Owners Thread/Forum) that the Elise is still not "for sure dead"...<P>In other words, there's still hope for late 2002 or possibly 2003!!!<P>Keep hope alive, Man!<P>As for my Lotus, I LOOOOOOVE IT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The only drawback is that they are spendy to repair if you let the maintenance go.  If not, they run fast and hard... forever!<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000056||Slammed Fiero||10-31-2001||01:17 PM||||A guy in our club has an 87 Esprit for sale 30 grand canadian. the motor has been rebuilt , clean car. Great track car , terrible autocross car. More at home on the open road. <P>very quirky car , as with most exotic cars, miss the required service and it's toast. If you buy a car like that you best make sure you have an extra 5 grand per year for. maintenance.<P>The esprit is a quick car , but for the money (about 1/2 the cost of a used esprit) you can go get a nice clean c4 vette , spend a few  bucks on the suspension and have a car that will be quicker and more reliable than the lotus..<P>JM <P>||||reg||1
