Z||000060||sloth85GT||10-31-2001||02:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sloth85GT:<BR><B>For the cost of an NSX, it's a waste. I hate Honda cars with a passion, they're scared to use some REAL horsepower. If they put a V8 in it, I'm sure it would be a 3.6L V8 or something like that so that it can be "ecenomical". It's not a super car, a super car is one that tops out about 400HP stock and can turn on a dime. All in can do is the turning part. The chassis has potential, they had to screw it up with a V6. For people that want to buy NSX's, get a Viper! Or even a Vetter and go see Mr. Lingenfelter with your extra cash.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You guys, I don't know what I was thinking, bad mood at the time I guess, but basically, I just don't like the car and don't think that it's worth the money. That's all. Apologize if it seemed like I was starting a flame war, no flames intended.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000061||danny boy||10-31-2001||05:05 PM|||| Who's EDSB52? For that matter,who's Rush Lim-whoever?<BR> Look, I witnessed with my own eyes a Stock C5 corvette 6 sp (not a Z06) run a 12.98. Now, pulling out R&T Sept,01, they say 13.6.<BR> I also saw a Viper R/T Run consistant high 13s/ low 14s. Magazine editors can't run 1/4 miles apparently.<BR> Here's a timeslip of mine. If what is in print is set in stone and the way it is, then I must be faster than Every Acura (tied the NSX), all the BMWs, every roadcar except Z06 Chevrolet makes, Ferrari456, all the Jags, all Mercedes(except CLKGTR), Porsche everything except911 turbo, RUF 3400S,  and am a tenth of a second slower than the fastest Mustang. Best stock 3000GT (with timeslip to back it up is right there with me. So you see, I have acual proof, not what some stupid magazine says.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/13.3_slip.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by danny boy (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000062||Master_Sushi||10-31-2001||05:54 PM||||Hey TRiAD!<P>Leave Rush Limbaugh out of this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">!!!<P>Or else...||||reg||10
Z||000063||TRiAD||10-31-2001||08:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by danny boy:<BR><B>Look, I witnessed with my own eyes a Stock C5 corvette 6 sp (not a Z06) run a 12.98. Now, pulling out R&T Sept,01, they say 13.6...yadda yadda</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Funny, some people say the cars are WAY faster than the mags, and others say the mags make them too fast, to aid advertisers. <P>You can<B>NOT</B> have it both ways. You're all paranoid.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000064||lou_dias||11-01-2001||12:31 PM||||The mags usually test new cars fresh from the factory.<BR>My little brother's LS1 98 TA did a 13.4 1/4 bone stock.<P>He changed tires and did 13.2<BR>remove a restriction in his airbox and put in a cutout on his exhaust and did a 12.94<P>Before he put in the cutout, he dynoed at 304HP at the wheels after the engine was "broken in".  Gee isn't is supposed to make 305 at the flywheel new?<P>My point, I'm sure a magazine will run a car say a new TA and state a time of 13.4, but run that car 20k miles later and it may be faster.  Also, stock tires SUCK!||||reg||1
Z||000065||Fie Ro||11-01-2001||04:05 PM||||I think there's a fundamental difference between American and Nonamerican cars.<P>Cubic inches verses roadability.<BR>(Fiero is quite Nonamerican in this comparison!)<P>But when I say around here I have a 2.8 V6 people always think I have at least 200BHP. Compared to a volkswagen VR6 for example which is quite common here.<P>* Nononono this is not a fast car, it just looks nice/different/exotic and it has a nice sound but please don't race me! ;-))) *<P>Lets face it, american cars are build for straight-line and european cars for driving. I once drove a 911 to southern France and I didn't knew I was cruising relaxed at 140mph until I was looking at the gauge.....Wowwwww back-off a bit! ;-) (ok, for a while!)<P>I like a Fiero because its different here and it has its own caracter for sure, but if I was into real FAST PERFORMANCE I wouldn't buy american cars.<BR>Some people have fun making lots of HP out of small engines. I know someone who has (=had, he has a 911 now, another one than I mentioned) a 1.8L volkswagen Corrado fitted with a Mercedes Compressor (or turbo, not sure) and he was adding a supercharger; at low revs the SC should be working, at higher rpms the turbo would kick in and the SC would be disengaged. It was a kind of experiment but it was 300-350 HP I can recall.But he is mad! ;-)))<P>So you can have different approaches: <BR>- big engine-heavy car<BR>- small engine-light car<BR>succes depending on the kind of racing, big (torque) engines need weight to keep traction so that wont work on a light car either. It's just the right combination. And that's what you pay for. In the case of a Fiero though you have a lot of possibilities but also a lot of work! ;-))))<P>Even a Corvette is not considered as a "real" sportscar here, spinning tires and lack of traction are still associated only to american cars....<P>The movies are mostly guilty of that "image" I think so. lets change that; gimme a nice 3.4 or 3.8 SC ;-))<P>------------------<BR>-The Beauty & The Beast-<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero GT & <BR>1977 Dodge W200||||reg||6
Z||000066||NeadleMeyer||12-08-2001||05:26 PM||||Hi all,<P>I am getting a 91-94 NSX very very soon.<BR>Can't wait||||reg||1
Z||000067||California Kid||12-08-2001||05:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NeadleMeyer:<BR><B>Hi all,<P>I am getting a 91-94 NSX very very soon.<BR>Can't wait</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Too bad.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000068||stingant0||12-08-2001||06:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B> Believe what you want. Any time I've tested a car in the same conditions and level of tune as R&T, I've come very close. You can say all you want, but I'll take my experiences, and an internationally published magazine over your "my car can do 0-60 3 seconds faster than they say" crap. <BR>BTW, You're a big Rush Limbaugh fan, aren't you? ...Or are you EdsB52 in disguise?!<BR>"It's all a conspiracy". whatever. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well R&T are not always right. They say that a stock T/A runs high 13's, well at Cordovan I saw (and have it on tape) a guy that just bought a new T/A automatic, he took out the air filter and ran a 13.2; that was the fastest run he made because they kicked him out because you have to wear a helmet if you go over 100 mph (he didn't have one) So I beleive that there are Monday and Friday engines, but every once and a while you will get a wendsday engine (like my mom--00 Lumina w/3.1 getting 37.5 mpg on the highway)||||reg||1
Z||000069||artherd||12-09-2001||01:39 AM||||Coool, they're like Fieros, only built well, and reliable!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NeadleMeyer:<BR><B>Hi all,<P>I am getting a 91-94 NSX very very soon.<BR>Can't wait</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000070||lowCG||12-11-2001||10:44 PM||||My next rod project is Japanese;the all aluminum V8 is just too cool to pass up,and I need a good driver so I don't get used to the Fiero(keeps it exciting).<BR>I just couldn't do another FWD car,so...<BR>The Lexus SC400,with upcoming supercharger,will make around 375-400hp@6psi.,plus,the car shares it's suspension with the Twin TurboSupra,so some kids original suspension(that he replaced with Eibachs)will replace my mushy springs here in a couple weeks,and my new 17s are the size that came on the TT car also.The Supra's huge brakes will bolt right on too. <BR>The Fiero(3.4dohc)is a sports car,the Lex is a luxury coupe,I wouldn't want to try and combine them and have something like the NSX,but that's just me.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000071||grinthock||12-12-2001||09:38 AM||||Slammed makes some good points, and I agree, the viper, is not that impressive, the only impressive part about it is the marketing campaign.  Saw a stock one turn high 13's, then after some mods turning mid 12's that's it....<P>Saw and have been in a NSX (not as the driver) very impressive.<P>I just wish we had engines more like the F 360 Mod, drove one last summer and WOW, the powerband was never ending, there wasn't one spot on the tach where the car seemed like it wasn't pulling at full potential....<P>Why can't WE do that!||||reg||1
