Z||000073||RedHaze86SD4||12-12-2001||11:18 AM||||Hey guys, Well I'm not a fan of the NSX at all and I've driven a Lotus Esprit v8 turbo and all i gotta say is DAAAMNNNN  But even in driving that thing theres something "wrong" can't say what it is but theres a feeling that just aint right. I prefer Fiero's but the Esprit is definately a nice car. As for the NSX's a friend of mine just lost his 94 NSX type-s, 3.0 turbo that dyno'd at 330hp stock with a ram air direct setup, a free flow exhaust the dyno was hitting 370hp. he ran a 1/4 at 113mph in 12.7 before the exhuast and then at 124 in 11.9 after the mods. course the last time was with street slicks so what thats .5 right there right?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> j/k||||reg||5
Z||000074||Turbo88||12-12-2001||05:52 PM||||Hehehe, looks like a brutal thread! I didn't read all the way through it; just wanted to throw up a post with my thoughts on the original intention of the thread. <P>*Me, Myself, and I* believe the NSX is an increadible waste of money. Yes, they handle exceptionally well, have some unique designs and are a mid engine car. Being a mod type person, I look at things in the bang for buck sorta way! For the cost of a new NSX, you can make a Fiero do doughnuts around it in any for of racing you choose. If you are in to new cars, you can buy a Z06 vette and compete close enough to it in most forms of racing that driver skill could be the deciding factor..... for about 1/2 the price. If ya got around 90k burning a hole in your pocket, concider a used F355. Once again, I am a mod man so I look at an NSX and think to myself, what could I do to another car that would cause it to out perform the NSX. Can I do it for less money than it would cost me just to buy an NSX. What is my ultimate goal? If performance isn't an issue but you just want to by an exotic car (and an NSX fits the bill) then it would be the car for you. *I* recall reading the aren't high maintenence supermodels of the exotic world like a Ferrari or Lambo. That means it might be a little more fun to own. <P>If you ask me where my discontent with the NSX comes from, then answer is, I beat one in straight line racing down a dry, clean street, this fall in a 1999 LS1 powered Pontiac Trans Am. The T/A had the free egr mod, and free ram air mod detailed in LS1.com . It was otherwise stock. I can't attest to driver skill but my automatic car ran slightly faster than him solidly pulled away every time he shifted. We ran from the 30mph starting point clear up to 75 where I cut off. <P>The best time slip I've pulled on my T/A at the crap local track was 13.62@ 106mph. I paid 19,200 dollars for my T/A used. I don't know what year the NSX was or what condition the drive train was in but I would estimate he would run a high 13.7. ||||reg||1
Z||000075||2xsess||12-12-2001||07:26 PM||||I like the NSX..because it's mid engined like the Fiero and I love the styling even if some of you think it's dated.<P>Here's an..um..interesting one I found..<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/80595517_003501_240x179.jpg"> <BR>Gag!!<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">           <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000076||ejayerik||12-12-2001||07:56 PM||||I drove an NSX once in Malibu on PCH. Unfortunately, it was an automatic. But the tork was great. However, I noticed the rear-end was squirly on the turns. I didn't like that one bit because if you know PCH..you know if you oversteer the turn your in the water. <BR> My boss has an 88 espirit Turbo Anniversary edition #33 of 88 sitting in the lot at work. It is a VERY good looking car. Even though it is only a 4 cyl, I would buy it in a flash if he was selling. He is just letting the thing sit there and rot! The rotors are rusted to the brake calipers! GRRRR That peves me sooo much that he only owns it for bragging rights. Nice car, but if you are over six foot tall, forget it. You won't fit. ||||reg||10
